WEBVTT

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:04.350
This is an astrology decision tool with two agents.

00:00:04.460 --> 00:00:09.290
One measures, the other interprets, and keeping them apart is what keeps it honest.

00:00:10.810 --> 00:00:14.420
There's no account, no email, and no password.

00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:17.940
You get an anonymous chart-self, kept on this machine.

00:00:18.010 --> 00:00:21.040
A hosted reader is optional, and I'm skipping it.

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:24.630
This birth moment is made up for the video.

00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:26.130
With no birth time,

00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:30.350
the app holds back the rising sign and the midheaven instead of guessing them,

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:32.270
and it says what that costs.

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:36.230
The birthplace resolves offline, down to its time zone.

00:00:37.580 --> 00:00:39.590
It gives me an anonymous handle.

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:43.010
Then it benchmarks this laptop and recommends the largest

00:00:43.060 --> 00:00:47.630
local model that will actually fit: a fourteen-billion-parameter model.

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:49.870
Nothing downloads until you say so.

00:00:50.890 --> 00:00:54.140
Before any reading, I switch the source to the local template,

00:00:54.190 --> 00:00:56.620
so nothing is written by a hosted model.

00:00:56.810 --> 00:01:00.400
Then I run the seeded demo: five real companies,

00:01:00.450 --> 00:01:03.960
each scored against the chart from the day it went public.

00:01:04.010 --> 00:01:07.180
Every reading carries a badge naming what wrote it.

00:01:08.410 --> 00:01:13.720
Backstage is the measurer's work: every aspect between the two charts, with its orb,

00:01:13.770 --> 00:01:18.620
and the order the tools ran in, which is fixed in code, not left to a model.

00:01:18.670 --> 00:01:21.200
The interpreter only reads those measures back,

00:01:21.250 --> 00:01:24.140
and if you ask whether to buy, it won't tell you.

00:01:25.620 --> 00:01:29.990
One agent measures, the other interprets, and neither does the other's job.

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:32.770
It's for reflection, not advice.
